  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shelter and Non-Food Item Humanitarian Assistance for Displaced Populations in Situation of Vulnerability in the Regions of Tahoua and Tillaberi in Niger</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In June 2021, the Government of Niger launched the relocation program for internally displaced persons in their areas of origin. This program aims to encourage the return of displaced populations to their areas of origin. In Tillab&#xe9;ri and Tahoua, population movements fleeing insecurity and violence perpetrated by non-state armed groups have increased despite government commitments to strengthen security around borders. This allocation allows IOM, as co-leader of the Shelter and Non-Food Items Working Group (GTABNA), led by the Ministry of Humanitarian Action and Disaster Management (MAH/GC), to provide emergency shelter and non-food item assistance to displaced persons in vulnerable situations in Tillab&#xe9;ri and Tahoua regions.</narrative>
  </description>
